    "episodeSummary": "A 68-year-old male with a history of coronary artery disease, prior MI, hyperlipidemia, and type 2 diabetes experienced sudden loss of consciousness, preceded by crescendo chest pain and ST elevation. He was found to be pulseless with arterial line flatlining. The rhythm is ventricular fibrillation. Labs show elevated troponin (1.85 ng/mL) and CK-MB (48 ng/mL), high lactate (4.8 mmol/L), low pH (7.21), and hyperglycemia (212 mg/dL). Electrolytes (potassium, magnesium) are within normal limits.",
